---
title: Belted kingfisher
---
# Belted kingfisher

The belted kingfisher is the common kingfisher of North America, shaggy-crested
and slate blue, the female more brightly marked than the male. It hunts from a
perch above clear water and catches fish with a headlong plunge, returning at
once to the branch to beat the fish senseless before swallowing it head-first.
Where perches are lacking it will hover and plunge from the hover instead. The
burrow is excavated in a vertical earth bank. See [[alcedinidae]].
